n R-leaning state", "Prediction markets uniformly price Sand near 84%", "Sand's extensive town-hall outreach building cross-party support"], "rationale": "Every recent poll shows Rob Sand ahead, including surveys from Republican-leaning firms, and the polling average sits around seven points. Markets and most expert raters treat Sand as the clear favorite, though Iowa's Republican lean and an open-seat dynamic keep some uncertainty.", "watch": "A late debate stumble or a consolidation of Republican voters behind Lahn in the final weeks could tighten the race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Kim Reynolds (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Iowa's governorship is open with Kim Reynolds retiring, and State Auditor Rob Sand has emerged as a strong Democratic contender in a state that usually favors Republicans. Polling since August consistently shows Sand leading Zach Lahn by margins of three to twelve points, including surveys from Republican-affiliated firms, with the overall average near seven points. Sand has run an intensive campaign, completing two 99-county town hall tours and drawing large crowds.\n\nLahn has campaigned on economic themes such as steel mill incentives and data center tax policy, and Republican-aligned outlets have attacked Sand as wealthy and out of touch. Prediction markets price Sand's chances around 84 percent, and most expert raters call the race a Democratic flip, though a couple rate it closer to a tossup. The state's Republican baseline keeps the race from being rated safe.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8753, "margin": 5.7}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8859, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8669, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8657, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8472, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8297, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8734, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8592, "mar